From: Batman <yellow.winson@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] batman: enable the memory cgroup controller on Pi 4 (#159/#98)

Drop cgroup_disable=memory from the bcm2711 /chosen bootargs so the memory
cgroup controller is available, letting docker enforce --memory on payload
containers (#98). Upstream 950-1349 removed the RPi implicit cgroup_disable
("memory"), so on this tree the DTS bootargs token is the ONLY thing turning
memcg off; removing it is sufficient and matches the DTB byte-patch validated
on manet01. This touches a .dtsi only -> just the DTB is recompiled, the kernel
binary and vermagic (6.6.138~42a5f0cc) are unchanged, so out-of-tree kmods
stay ABI-compatible.

Signed-off-by: Batman <yellow.winson@gmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-ds.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-ds.dtsi
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 
 / {
 	chosen {
-		bootargs = "coherent_pool=1M 8250.nr_uarts=1 snd_bcm2835.enable_headphones=0 cgroup_disable=memory numa_policy=interleave";
+		bootargs = "coherent_pool=1M 8250.nr_uarts=1 snd_bcm2835.enable_headphones=0 numa_policy=interleave";
 	};
 
 	__overrides__ {
